  "description": "**As a** Shopper, \n\n**I want** to filter products using a responsive filter panel on the PLP, \n\n**so that** I can quickly narrow down to the products most relevant to me.\n\n----\n\n**Image for reference (Figma leading):**\n\n![\"image-20260722-232958.png\"](image-20260722-232958.png)\n\n![\"image-20260729-034755.png\"](image-20260729-034755.png)\n\n![\"image-20260723-042116.png\"](image-20260723-042116.png)\n\nNo result state + “Clear All” option added:\n\n![\"image-20260729-072426.png\"](image-20260729-072426.png)\n\n\n\nThis story covers the PWA build of the filter panel as consumed on the Product Listing Page (PLP), it is a shared filter panel component like in SFCC-108. It scopes the integration of that component into the PLP page template, including category-level facet rendering specific to PLP, and confirms the filter panel behaves correctly in the PLP context.",
  "comments": [
    {
      "id": "13575",
      "body": "Hi User:712020:95338d1d-c86b-4b96-9d93-2435154f753f \n\nA couple of things I wanted to check before I approve this one:\n\n1. You reference a “Clear all” button - I think the designs need to be updated to reflect this\n1. I think that a client should be able to view the selected facet values within the slide out at the top for quick reference and an easy way to remove them without reopening the facet again.\n1. Within the availability filter/ facet I think it would be worth while referencing the option for “Coming soon” - if a client choose to select coming soon then and products that are unavailable but either “back in soon” or “coming soon” should be returned.\n\nUser:712020:4ec4770e-9470-4885-9753-69a36b6cf950 - take a look and let me know if I have missed anything\n\nUser:5cc71886cbbec211ec62929d User:600810992b411b0076aaf4cc",
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Emma Kirwan",
        "name": "Emma Kirwan",
        "email": null,
        "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/437c30dd63bbb0ec0a2f7c0d8d556d93?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FEK-4.png"
      },
      "created": "2026-07-29T13:29:59.674+1000",
      "updated": "2026-07-29T13:29:59.674+1000"
    },
    {
      "id": "13576",
      "body": "Hi User:712020:c99d37b3-9c93-4347-951d-5ffb32ff1341 \n\n1. The button in the designs just says clear (which will clear all of the applied filters) - I've updated the AC to be consistent.\n1. I've added another screenshot of the design; the selected filters are highlighted when the modal is open (and they're also visible at top of the page when the modal is closed as shown in the other screenshot). This behaviour is captured by AC 6 - let me know if this covers what you're after.\n1. I've added an AC to capture the \"Coming Soon\" behaviour - AC 10.\n\nLet me know if anything else needs changing",
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Bianca Morley",
        "name": "Bianca Morley",
        "email": "bianca.morley@accenture.com",
        "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3ed5cb479d913eb2e6c6e873c040c0d5?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBM-4.png"
      },
      "created": "2026-07-29T13:54:16.400+1000",
      "updated": "2026-07-29T13:54:16.400+1000"
    },
    {
      "id": "13579",
      "body": "User:712020:95338d1d-c86b-4b96-9d93-2435154f753f \n\n1.  I was saying that I think there should be a clear all option on the PLP, not in the slide out - I it should sit to the LHS of the selected filters.\n\n![\"image-20260729-051352.png\"](image-20260729-051352.png)\n\n1. this is fine\n1. thank you for updating\n\nUser:5cc71886cbbec211ec62929d User:600810992b411b0076aaf4cc",
      "author": {
